  Slug: sense-of-belonging
  DisplayName: Sense of Belonging
  IconPath: systems/pf2e/icons/default-icons/background.svg
  Description: Home is all you've ever wanted. But home, whatever that means to you,
    has always been a step out of reach. On the night of the Missing Moment, you
    saw loving figures with outstretched arms, beckoning you toward a warm hearth
    just inside a glowing archway. On the other side of the portal, though, you found
    only missing memories and lost time, your feet back at the very spot where you
    started. Perhaps your heart was broken that night, or perhaps you met your mission
    to find a suitable community with renewed zeal. Either way, you haven't felt
    quite "whole" since your gatewalker experience. Your new ability to momentarily
    disappear onto another plane of existence only reinforces this feeling of emptiness.
    Your deviant abilities are of the wraith classification. You gain the @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.feats-srd.Item.Eerie
    Flicker] deviant feat. As a quirk, whenever you use a deviant ability, plants
    around you spontaneously bloom and then wilt, as if rapidly aging. Choose two
    attribute boosts. One must be to Constitution or Intelligence , and one is a
    free attribute boost. You're trained in the Survival skill and the Scouting Lore
    skill. You gain the @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.feats-srd.Item.Forager] skill feat.
  SourceTitle: Pathfinder Gatewalkers Player's Guide
